      "content": "While I understand your concerns, taking extra-strength ibuprofen and monitoring your symptoms at home may not be enough to fully assess your condition. A safe way to monitor the situation would be to watch for signs of increased redness, swelling, pus, or red streaks from the cut spreading further. If you notice any severe swelling, redness, or difficulty moving your arm, seek help immediately. Even if you can't see immediate improvement, ensure you clean the cut and apply antibiotic ointment and a bandage to prevent further infection.",
